{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.BorromeanH4CategoricalDerivation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.BorromeanH4CategoricalDerivation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Coeff","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromean_h4_numeric_factorisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromean_h4_numeric_factorisation","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-h4-categorical-derivation.lean#L98-L117","doc":"**Numeric factorisation lemma** for the Borromean h⁴ coefficient:\nthe `h⁴` coefficient of the `(2,1)` character, times the `(2,1)`\nMarkov–Wenzl weight at the symmetric point, is `−3/4`.\n\n**This was previously stated as `(-3 : ℝ) * (1/4 : ℝ) = -3/4`, proved\nby `norm_num`** — a true arithmetic fact that mentions nothing in the\nframework and would still hold if either factor came from somewhere\nelse entirely. The statement now names both inputs, so it is false if\nthe character polynomial or the weight closed form is wrong: that is\nthe falsifiability AGENTS.md §\"Derive-then-check\" asks for before a\nproof is attempted.\n\nWhat is still NOT proved here is the composition — that this product\nIS `h⁴(tr_M(β_Bor))`. That needs q-Schur duality plus Markov-trace\nexistence and is stated as the deferred theorem in the comment\nbelow. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:borromean-h4-categorical-derivation","label":"prop:borromean-h4-categorical-derivation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-h4-categorical-derivation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.yTwoOne_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.yTwoOne_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-h4-categorical-derivation.lean#L94-L96","doc":"At the symmetric point `q = 1`, `[2]_q = 2` and `y_(2,1) = 1/4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chiTwoOneBorromean_coeff_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chiTwoOneBorromean_coeff_four","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-h4-categorical-derivation.lean#L90-L92","doc":"The `h⁴` coefficient of `χ^{(2,1)}(β_Bor)` is `−3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.yTwoOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.yTwoOne","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-h4-categorical-derivation.lean#L86-L88","doc":"The `(2,1)` Markov–Wenzl weight in closed form,\n`y_(2,1)(q) = 1/[2]_q²` (`prop:h3-markov-wenzl-weights`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInt2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInt2","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-h4-categorical-derivation.lean#L83-L84","doc":"The symmetric q-integer `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chiTwoOneBorromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chiTwoOneBorromean","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-h4-categorical-derivation.lean#L77-L81","doc":"The `(2,1)` character of the Borromean braid as a polynomial in `h`:\n`χ^{(2,1)}(β_Bor) = 2 − 3h⁴ − h⁶`, supplied by the q-heat-kernel\nPeter–Weyl decomposition (`prop:q-heat-kernel-peter-weyl`,\n`prop:habiro-residue-sum-equivalence`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}